WEBVTT

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.510
Yes! It's going to get canceled for sure!

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:13.520
By next week, I'll have my energy back,
so Chisato won't take my place on the mound!

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:16.870
Shigeno Daigo

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:19.900
Ah, it's Daigo.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:21.170
Hello?

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:22.320
Good morning!

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:24.170
What?

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.000
The game's going ahead?!

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:02.720
<b>Semi-Finals Time!</b>

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:02.720
The organizers of the tournament said
this rain isn't enough for them to cancel.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.180
Apparently, it's supposed 
to let up around noon.

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:09.400
So why can't we wait for it
to stop and then play?

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.840
I'll leave the rest to you, Shigeno-kun.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:12.520
Right.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.890
These conditions aren't the best,
but it's the same for both teams.

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:21.200
It would've been nice to
have some time to rest up,

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.370
but let's get fired up
and do our best out there.

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:26.870
Mifune Baseball Park

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:26.440
Okay, time for today's batting lineup.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:30.520
Leadoff to third will
stay the same as before:

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:32.710
Chisato, Tao, and Sawa-san.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:39.550
Since Anita's wrist is injured, I'll play
cleanup and wear the mask today.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.760
That's some load you're carrying, captain.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.990
Since he did well last time out,
batting fifth, Nishina, right field.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:47.600
Yeah, there it is!

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:50.250
Batting sixth, Anita, left field.

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:54.000
Batting seventh, Tanba-san, first base.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:54.650
Got it.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.170
Batting eighth, Kandori, third base.

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:01.020
The questionable 6-hole has
finally dropped down the order.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.790
<i>I guess Chisato will be pitching first.</i>

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:10.240
<i>Well, after yesterday's pitching practice,</i>

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:13.180
<i>it's obvious it'll be either
her or Nishina on the mound.</i>

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:18.700
Batting ninth and last, Mutsuko,
so she won't have to bat so much.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:20.990
And naturally, she's our starting pitcher.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:23.510
All right, let's go!

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:25.350
Huh?!

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:29.310
<b>Yanagawa</b>

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:29.310
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:29.310
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:33.460
All right.

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:33.900
Oops.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:37.290
Sorry!

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:41.360
I see how it is.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:45.030
I'm surprised this team managed to win twice.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:48.100
Ain't this a sign that
they've got a good pitcher?

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:53.120
Nope. Their #1 and #10 were pitching yesterday...

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:56.970
...and it was like that.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:57.500
So slow!

00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:00.060
Looks like this'll be an easy win.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:02.190
No. We can't let our guard down.

00:04:02.690 --> 00:04:05.340
If we're just going on speed, 
our ace isn't any faster.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.350
It seems the luck of the
draw got them this far,

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.310
but underestimating them could be fatal.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:15.030
Let's keep our heads, get a clean win,

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:16.900
and progress to the final this afternoon.

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:18.900
Line up!

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:20.610
Bow!

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:22.790
Good luck!

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:31.680
H-Hold up, Daigo.

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:33.040
Huh?

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:35.500
Why are you putting me in from the start?

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.480
I thought you'd put 
Chisato on the mound first,

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:40.860
since I'm tired from
pitching two days in a row.

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:43.530
I never said I'd do that.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:47.500
What I said was we'd get both
of you pitching against Yanagawa.

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:52.470
I don't know how much your body
was able to recover in just one night.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:57.940
You'll pitch from the start, but as soon 
as fatigue sets in, we'll switch to Chisato.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.970
I'll keep an eye out for that as well.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:05.170
B-But Chisato's pitches are way faster,
and she has experience...

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:08.860
Pitching isn't about how fast
you can throw it, Mutsuko.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:16.400
<i>First inning, Yanagawa Middle to bat.</i>

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:16.750
<b>Yanagawa</b>

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:16.750
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:16.750
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:20.090
<i>Batting first, shortstop, Hasegawa-kun.</i>

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:21.460
Play ball!

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:25.560
The most important thing
in pitching is control,

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:28.340
and the mental strength to
maintain that control at all times.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:30.600
Strike!

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:34.560
You have a firm handle on both.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:39.730
Foul!

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:43.140
Chisato may be experienced,
but she's a middle relief pitcher.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:46.550
We have no idea about her stamina,
or how she performs as a starting pitcher.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:52.710
But we do know that, despite everything,
you've gotten us through the last two games,

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:54.280
and you're getting better and better.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:02.090
Navigating tight spots and keeping it
together in your very first tournament

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:04.090
requires a lot of mental strength.

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:07.700
Have more faith in yourself, Mutsuko.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:13.850
Strike three! Out!

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:15.690
Nice one!

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:21.700
Well, look at you, little miss chirpy.

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:23.440
Looking good, Mutsu!

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:27.530
<i>Batting second, right field, Tanimura-kun.</i>

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:25.940
<i>Yer one tough cookie, Senpai.</i>

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:33.530
Strike! You're out!

00:06:35.340 --> 00:06:37.010
Two outs!

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:40.210
Huh. Doesn't look like I'm needed, after all.

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:44.860
<i>Batting third, left field, Nakamori-kun.</i>

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:48.340
<i>Well, luck got us this far,</i>

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:50.530
<i>but I guess when you get to the semi-finals,</i>

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:53.140
<i>you won't face a team nice
enough to give you gimmes.</i>

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:57.810
Strike!

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:01.310
<i>Mutsuko's in good form.</i>

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:05.770
<i>I guess she's the type of pitcher who recovers
quickly and gets better the more she pitches.</i>

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:06.730
<i>I can do this.</i>

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:12.110
<i>I don't feel tired at all and against
these guys, I can win this by myself!</i>

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:14.490
Got it!

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:16.080
Huh?

00:07:19.270 --> 00:07:20.080
Safe!

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:22.180
Sorry, my bad.

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:23.430
It's okay.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:28.840
<i>Batting fourth, third base, Kimura-kun.</i>

00:07:34.310 --> 00:07:35.010
Second!

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:41.360
Hey, c'mon! What the hell are you doing?

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:45.300
All right! Two outs, first and third!

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:47.520
<i>Looks like our team hasn't run out of luck yet.</i>

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:49.690
I'm sorry, Mutsuko.

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:51.240
It's fine, don't worry!

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:55.500
<i>Batting fifth, second base, Sakai-kun.</i>

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:58.110
<i>Both made errors even though
they're usually good in the field.</i>

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:02.920
<i>The rain's making the
 ball behave differently,</i>

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:05.020
<i>which makes bad hops more likely.</i>

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:08.590
<i>The ground's pretty messed up because
of both teams' drills before the game.</i>

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:11.030
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:17.810
Got it!

00:08:19.070 --> 00:08:19.520
Uh-oh.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:20.270
Seriously?

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.730
Yeah! We took the lead!

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:25.890
We all thought we had it, huh?

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:27.160
I'm sorry.

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:30.290
Next time that happens,
I'll make sure I get to it.

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:31.940
Sounds good!

00:08:32.170 --> 00:08:35.910
<i>Batting sixth, first base, Takanashi-kun.</i>

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:35.910
Two outs!

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:37.910
Runners on first and third again!

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:41.620
<b>Yanagawa</b>

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:41.620
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:41.620
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:40.550
<i>This can't be happening!</i>

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:42.000
<i>I'm pitching well,</i>

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.290
<i>so why is it going down like this?</i>

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:46.750
Ball!

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:48.840
Ball!

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:56.300
Ball!

00:08:57.190 --> 00:08:59.170
<i>Seriously, what's going on?</i>

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:03.640
<i>The ball's wet from the rain and
I'm having trouble controlling it!</i>

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:06.290
Mutsuko! Use the rosin bag!

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:08.360
It's in your back pocket!

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:09.940
It'll stop it from slipping!

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:12.120
<i>Ah! I forgot all about that.</i>

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:15.420
<i>I've never really used it before.</i>

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:22.910
Play!

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:26.210
Come on. Get it together.

00:09:26.570 --> 00:09:28.920
Ya got this, Senpai!

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:31.380
<i>Good luck, Mutsuko.</i>

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.050
Strike!

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:38.180
Strike two!

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:41.470
You're out!

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:42.750
Three outs!

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:45.810
Awesome!

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:46.770
Nice pitching!

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:52.980
<i>She needed rosin, but she got us out of that
tight spot with three consecutive strikes.</i>

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:55.630
Yeah, let's turn it around from here!

00:09:53.870 --> 00:09:56.480
<i>Her ability to self-correct 
and her guts on the mound</i>

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:59.680
<i>may be way better than even I was expecting.</i>

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:03.440
We're lucky we've got Mutsuko, huh?

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:07.910
You said it. Our errors were
about to cost us a ton of runs.

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:09.780
Senpai.

00:10:12.700 --> 00:10:14.430
What's up, Anita?

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:19.580
Oh, uh, y-ya know, 
yer the linchpin of our defense,

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:21.970
so ya gotta tighten up
an' be a bit more solid.

00:10:22.460 --> 00:10:24.010
We already know that.

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:25.500
But what can we do?

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:27.600
The ground conditions are really bad.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:29.960
Sorry about that. We'll be more careful.

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:32.440
That run was totally on us.

00:10:35.370 --> 00:10:36.930
<i>Bottom of the first.</i>

00:10:36.930 --> 00:10:39.150
<i>Fuurin Academy to bat.</i>

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:42.510
<i>Batting first, center field, Fujii-san.</i>

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:44.120
All right! Go!

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:48.210
Against this loser pitcher,
one run is nothing!

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:49.190
Hey!

00:10:49.190 --> 00:10:51.330
You'll get us a warning from the umpire.

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:52.730
Play!

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:00.970
Strike!

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:07.520
Hm? Did you say something, Anita?

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:10.230
I'm talkin' 'bout yesterday, ya know?

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:15.050
Shigeno-senpai wanted us
to watch Eihou's game.

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:17.190
So why'd y'all split?

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:19.350
Hm? What's wrong?

00:11:19.350 --> 00:11:21.910
Are you mad we left, Anita?

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:25.120
W-Well, I ain't exactly mad...

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:29.920
I mean, maybe it wasn't fair on
Daigo AKA Mr. Overenthusiastic,

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:33.580
but we thought watching
Eihou's game was pretty pointless.

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:40.970
Yes!

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:42.090
Nice batting!

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:45.880
<i>Batting second, shortstop, Sagara-san.</i>

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:48.060
Wh-Whaddaya mean, "pointless"?

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:50.020
Well, you know...

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:54.370
We're girls, after all.

00:11:54.370 --> 00:11:58.190
I mean, competing with the boys?
We should drop it while we can laugh it off.

00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:02.330
To be honest, the thought of
playing Eihou does nothing for me.

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:05.780
They're gonna demolish us 
and make us feel pathetic.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:10.370
Out!

00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:12.710
Out!

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:22.240
Huh. Maybe that was a ball after all.

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:24.960
Ya think?! Pay attention, you doofus!

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:29.420
Got it!

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:31.100
Out!

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:34.160
Three outs! Change sides!

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.900
<b>Yanagawa</b>

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.900
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.900
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:38.610
Those pitches are <i>so</i> slow.
It's hard to get a good hit.

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:42.240
They're so weak, they go nowhere
even when you do hit them.

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:44.450
Hey, you two.

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:48.300
Both the ones you swung at were balls.

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:50.810
I know it's tempting to swing
when they're that slow,

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:52.430
but pick your moment.

00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:54.120
Yeah, you're right.

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:55.910
Sorry, my bad.

00:12:58.300 --> 00:12:59.460
<i>Those errors earlier...</i>

00:12:59.940 --> 00:13:01.830
<i>It ain't the rain that caused 'em.</i>

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:06.340
<i>Those two couldn't care less 
'bout winnin' this game!</i>

00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:08.600
<i>I remember what they said.</i>

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:11.880
We should drop it while we can laugh it off.

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:17.040
They're going to demolish us 
and make us feel pathetic.

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:19.980
<i>An' they meant it, too.</i>

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:22.440
<i>If the backbone of our
 team has that attitude,</i>

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:25.570
<i>we ain't even gonna win the
games we should be winnin'!</i>

00:13:43.350 --> 00:13:46.800
<i>Batting second, shortstop, Sagara-san.</i>

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:48.170
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:49.390
<i>Only two innings left.</i>

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:53.460
<i>With a pitcher like that,
I figured runs would come easy.</i>

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:56.350
<i>I never imagined we'd have no
runs on the board by the fifth.</i>

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:59.180
Tao! Go get 'em!

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:00.250
Ah, we can do that.

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:05.180
You need to sit on the bench and rest up
as much as you can while we're batting.

00:14:05.180 --> 00:14:06.570
I'm fine, really.

00:14:07.020 --> 00:14:09.910
If we don't score some runs, we're going to lose!

00:14:10.190 --> 00:14:12.350
This isn't the time to space out in the back.

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:17.310
Tao! You can do this!

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:19.340
<i>Sakura-senpai's on her third straight game
pitchin' an' she's still goin' strong.</i>

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:25.680
<i>This is the innin' where the top
of the order needs to do somethin'!</i>

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:32.050
All right!

00:14:34.230 --> 00:14:35.020
Out!

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:39.600
Dang. That was a good hit, too.

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:44.380
<i>Batting third, second base, Sawa-san.</i>

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:47.280
<i>I thought Tao would make that for sure...</i>

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:48.990
<i>This is really bad.</i>

00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:51.450
<i>We need to do something this inning.</i>

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:53.250
<i>Or we'll have our backs to the wall.</i>

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:56.540
Sorry I couldn't get on base.

00:14:56.850 --> 00:15:00.250
It would've made it through
if it wasn't such a swamp out there.

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:05.210
So why didn't you start 
runnin' sooner, Sagara-senpai?

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:12.560
'Course ya won't make it if ya wait till
it bounces off his glove to start runnin'.

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:16.930
Are ya really fine with losin' this game?

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:20.780
Sakura-senpai's givin' it
all she's got out there.

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:23.230
Don't that mean anythin' to you?!

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:25.190
Ball!

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:34.280
You think Yayoi and me aren't giving it our
all 'cause of what we said earlier, Anita?

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:37.170
Well, what'm I s'posed to think?!

00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:39.200
Yer makin' errors and swingin' too early!

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:41.510
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:43.630
Hang on, Anita.

00:15:44.180 --> 00:15:48.830
You were slow to start running because
your foot slipped on the mud, right?

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:49.590
Yeah.

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:54.520
I heard what they said too,
but I figured it was just a joke.

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:57.310
I can't imagine either of them
wanting to lose on purpose.

00:15:57.820 --> 00:16:01.390
If they ain't ready to give it everythin' 
to win, it amounts to the same thing!

00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:03.280
What are you girls on about?

00:16:03.280 --> 00:16:04.640
It doesn't matter.

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:06.480
Just some girls' locker room talk.

00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:10.350
I'm sayin' it don't <i>look</i> like
you're givin' it your all out there!

00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:11.410
What?

00:16:11.410 --> 00:16:14.750
You've got some nerve saying
that when you've got no proof!

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:16.950
Proof? Oh, there's proof.

00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:18.700
Plenty o' proof!

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:23.410
You ain't done jack against
this crazy weak opponent!

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:25.420
If you'd at least done <i>somethin'</i>...

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:35.890
It's gone!

00:16:36.290 --> 00:16:37.430
Oh, yeah!

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:38.560
Yes!

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:46.860
We caught up!

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:50.720
There. We did something.

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:53.570
Now, stop accusing people 
of throwing the game.

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:57.980
<i>Batting fourth, catcher, Shigeno-kun.</i>

00:16:57.980 --> 00:16:59.220
<i>All right.</i>

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:01.200
<i>We'll get it done this inning.</i>

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:06.010
Sweet!

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:07.340
Way to go, Daigo!

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:11.050
<i>Batting fifth, right field, Nishina-kun.</i>

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:13.730
I'm going to finish this myself!

00:17:13.730 --> 00:17:14.760
Ow!

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:15.790
Hit by pitch!

00:17:15.790 --> 00:17:18.470
Hey, were you <i>that</i> afraid of my swing?!

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:17.360
Yay!

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:18.070
Rejoice.

00:17:18.070 --> 00:17:19.720
Now our chances are even better!

00:17:20.090 --> 00:17:21.080
Timeout.

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:22.560
We're changing pitchers.

00:17:24.050 --> 00:17:27.650
<i>Field change for Yanagawa Middle.</i>

00:17:27.970 --> 00:17:32.350
<i>Pitcher Oyama-kun is
replaced by Fukuzawa-kun.</i>

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:34.530
Hey, it looks like I might be up soon,
so can you two take over as base coaches?

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:36.960
Sure. I'll take first base.

00:17:36.960 --> 00:17:39.010
Yayoi, can you take third?

00:17:39.010 --> 00:17:39.950
Okay.

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:46.170
He's a left-hander like you, Chisato.

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:49.540
Doesn't seem like he's any
faster than their starting pitcher.

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:54.840
<i>Batting sixth, left field, Kabashima-san.</i>

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:56.320
Play!

00:17:58.020 --> 00:18:00.890
<i>Tied game, one out,
runners on first an' second.</i>

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:06.850
<i>After confrontin' 'em like that,
I can't afford to waste this.</i>

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:10.440
<i>Ripe for the hittin'!</i>

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:16.370
Strike!

00:18:16.370 --> 00:18:17.150
Huh?

00:18:17.690 --> 00:18:20.120
They're moving, Anita!

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:21.660
Keep your eye on the ball!

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:24.660
Hit it, hit it, Anita!

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:25.330
<i>It curved.</i>

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:27.540
<i>He hid that curveball 
when he was warmin' up.</i>

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:32.480
<i>I've caught Chisato's pitches before...</i>

00:18:33.220 --> 00:18:36.800
<i>But I ain't got a whole lotta experience
hittin' left-handed pitches.</i>

00:18:37.400 --> 00:18:40.300
<i>S'too late to realize that now!</i>

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:45.770
Weak.

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:47.810
Shortstop!

00:18:59.440 --> 00:19:00.490
Out!

00:19:03.590 --> 00:19:05.870
Hey— Anita, are you okay?

00:19:06.510 --> 00:19:09.830
You seriously dived
head-first on a day like this?

00:19:15.930 --> 00:19:17.290
I'm sorry.

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:19.420
That was pathetic.

00:19:24.580 --> 00:19:27.770
<i>Batting seventh, first base, Tanba-kun.</i>

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:30.350
Hang in there, Tanba-san!

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:36.820
So, thanks to Anita screwing up her hit,
it's up to our hopeless 7-hole and 8-hole.

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:43.280
<i>Th-They're walking me?</i>

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:43.760
Ball!

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:46.460
I guess it's because first is open.

00:19:46.460 --> 00:19:49.120
He does also look like
the biggest baseball nut.

00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:51.460
<i>Thank god!</i>

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:53.210
Ball!

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:55.250
Ball four.

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:58.420
Wow-ee. So now sumo girl is up?

00:19:59.140 --> 00:20:02.380
<i>Batting eighth, third base, Kandori-san.</i>

00:20:02.810 --> 00:20:04.320
Hey, Shigeno!

00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:05.530
I mean, captain!

00:20:05.530 --> 00:20:06.850
Timeout! Timeout!

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:08.460
Excuse me! Timeout!

00:20:08.460 --> 00:20:09.060
Timeout!

00:20:09.610 --> 00:20:10.540
What's up, Nishina?

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:11.690
Is something wrong?

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:14.270
You have to ask?
Are you even paying attention?!

00:20:14.730 --> 00:20:17.360
What's Sekitori gonna do here?

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:19.290
All she'll do is strike out.

00:20:19.290 --> 00:20:20.530
Do something!

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:21.610
S-Sekitori?

00:20:22.220 --> 00:20:24.300
Oh, you mean Kandori.

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:25.700
There's no need to do anything.

00:20:25.970 --> 00:20:27.040
What?

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:28.180
Don't worry.

00:20:28.180 --> 00:20:30.720
You can count on Kandori in this at-bat.

00:20:30.720 --> 00:20:31.820
What?

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:35.470
Are you done?

00:20:35.470 --> 00:20:36.640
Ah, I'm sorry!

00:20:36.640 --> 00:20:37.630
We're ready.

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:42.070
Hey, Anita, your face is covered in dirt!

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:43.390
You should go wash it.

00:20:43.390 --> 00:20:44.590
Huh? What?

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:46.800
Is it that dirty?

00:20:47.770 --> 00:20:48.680
Play!

00:20:58.600 --> 00:21:02.530
When she was new to the team,
she couldn't hit anything in the cages.

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:09.780
But then, we tried a left-handed machine
and found she could hit those really well.

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:19.040
Huh?

00:21:19.980 --> 00:21:20.460
Oh?

00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:30.140
You make fun of her
because you haven't seen it,

00:21:30.780 --> 00:21:33.850
but against left-handed 
pitchers, she's a real machine.

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:41.440
All right.

00:21:44.630 --> 00:21:46.080
Seriously?

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:50.700
Despite being a left-handed batter,
she's a southpaw killer.

00:21:57.160 --> 00:22:01.870
And none of us could figure out why.

00:22:04.510 --> 00:22:06.420
<b>Yanagawa</b>

00:22:04.510 --> 00:22:06.670
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:22:04.510 --> 00:22:06.670
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:22:16.130 --> 00:22:17.560
That's game.

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:28.970
Thank you!

00:24:00.680 --> 00:24:01.440
Huh?

00:24:01.440 --> 00:24:04.290
Isn't that Mayuwara Michiru-chan?

00:24:04.290 --> 00:24:06.210
What's she doing on this team?

00:24:06.210 --> 00:24:08.840
I guess she continued playing
in the rubber-ball leagues?

00:24:08.840 --> 00:24:10.720
It's been a while, Shigeno-kun.

00:24:11.060 --> 00:24:15.820
I've decided to take the crown 
with this team, with these people.

00:24:16.180 --> 00:24:18.920
I don't care who I go up 
against, I won't lose.

00:24:19.470 --> 00:24:21.520
Next time: "An Unexpected Reunion."

00:24:19.470 --> 00:24:24.980
<b>An Unexpected Reunion</b>

00:24:21.520 --> 00:24:23.760
Run to the stage of your dreams!
